🚽 Test case: round-21 review finding #1's exhibit B -- `skibidi *p;`
🚽 (no initializer) previously took the SAME parse-time crash path as
🚽 `skibidi x;` (create_default_node()'s VAR_VOID case), despite the
🚽 semantic analyzer explicitly distinguishing (VAR_VOID, 0) from
🚽 (VAR_VOID, 1) everywhere else -- create_default_node() never had the
🚽 opportunity to see pointer_level at all. This codebase has no general
🚽 uninitialized-pointer-default policy for ANY base type today, though
🚽 (`rizz *p;` alone already fails semantic analysis the same way,
🚽 confirmed independently), so a pointer-typed default now falls
🚽 through to the same plain-zero-node default every other pointer type
🚽 already uses, reaching that SAME, already-established semantic
🚽 rejection -- not a parse-time crash unique to void.
skibidi main {
    skibidi *p;
    bussin 0;
}
